  "independentFinding": "The June 17, 2025 APHIS program update explicitly assesses citrus black spot as confined to portions of eight southwest Florida counties. California is outside that dated authority distribution. Current California absence remains unresolved.",
  "limitations": [
    "The main only-found statement is under Quarantine Boundaries. Nonregulated means not known to occur; regulated requires federal confirmation.",
    "The directive is 448 days old and the shared page modification is 405 days old as of September 8, 2026. Retrieval does not renew either claim.",
    "Five changed counties are named, not the complete eight-county set; do not reconstruct the unnamed three.",
    "Disease distribution does not establish absence in imported fruit, transported material, suspect samples or exclusionary facilities.",
    "The exact former name Guignardia citricarpa is explicitly supported; unrelated genus records must fail."
  ],
